cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  tm-vocabulary: an event-dated USPTO trademark corpus and a two-sided measure
  of vocabulary position
message: >-
  If you use this software, the corpus build, or the data release, please cite
  the paper below. Derived panels containing patent counts additionally
  require attribution to PatentsView (CC-BY-4.0); see DATA_SOURCES.md.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Silver
    given-names: Eric
    email: epsilver@gmail.com
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3351-1109
repository-code: https://github.com/ericsilver/tm-vocabulary
url: https://aporia.institute/tm-vocabulary/
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
abstract: >-
  Re-parses all 13.99 million USPTO trademark case files into event-dated
  prosecution histories and scores every filing's goods/services description
  against what its industry filed in the five years before and the five years
  after. Atypicality is the average of the two divergences; lead is their
  signed difference.
keywords:
  - trademarks
  - innovation indicators
  - text as data
  - topic models
  - Kullback-Leibler divergence
  - USPTO
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: >-
    An event-dated corpus of US trademark prosecution and a two-sided measure
    of vocabulary position
  authors:
    - family-names: Silver
      given-names: Eric
      orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3351-1109
  year: 2026
  url: https://ssrn.com/abstract=7520758
  journal: SSRN Working Paper 7520758
